incision surgical approaches; and SpeedAkin Anatomic Compression Implant. In addition, the company offers The IntelliGuide patient specific instrumentation provides patient-specific, 3D-printed cut guides, and a pre-operative plan for a complete picture of the deformity and correction. Further, it provides FastGrafter Autografter Harvesting System; SpeedRelease Guided Release Instrument; TriTome Triple-Edge Release Instrument; RazorTome 7mm Precision Osteotome; LapiTome Hooked Bone Removal Osteotome; GreatRelease Rapid MTP Release Instrument; CornerChisel Release Tool; NanoRasp MIS Bone Contouring Tool; FeatherRasp Rapid Bone Contouring Instrument; and Akinator Single-cut Akin Wedge Osteotomy tool. Additionally, the company offers biologics and wedges, such as Treace Allograft Wedges; and CortiFuse Flowable Cortical Fibers. Treace Medical Concepts, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Ponte Vedra, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John T. Treace | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 53 | Compensation: $770,190 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 450 people. Revenue per employee of $473K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $75K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Treace Medical Concepts, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $345M market cap on $213M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -99% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 81% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $29M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -10.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 25% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 25% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7345823575331764},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 140% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.4M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Comparing Coloplast A/S (OTCMKTS:CLPBY) & Treace Medical Concepts (NASDAQ:TMCI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/comparing-coloplast-a-s-otcmktsclpby-treace-medical-concepts-nasdaqtmci.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493741.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Gagnon Securities LLC Buys 386,375 Shares of Treace Medical Concepts, Inc. $TMCI","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/gagnon-securities-llc-buys-386375-shares-of-treace-medical-concepts-inc-tmci.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475884.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Contrast: NeuroOne Medical Technologies (NASDAQ:NMTC) and Treace Medical Concepts (NASDAQ:TMCI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/financial-contrast-neuroone-medical-technologies-nasdaqnmtc-and-treace-medical-concepts-nasdaqtmci.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794302973.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Treace Medical Concepts (NASDAQ:TMCI) 